  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Deploy order",
      "items": [
        "furrow runs ensure → render → build → gate → stop → install → start",
        "build and gate land before the stop, so either failure leaves the old container running",
        "one build lane; a separate deploy-<service> lock bounds deploys",
        "a poke is a service, ref, sha and tree: never a path, and the box keeps no git state"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Gate and credentials",
      "items": [
        "a gated track will not start on a key that is missing, empty, EXAMPLE- or changeme",
        "the deploy still exits 0: the service is installed and waiting, and weedr service start re-checks",
        "systemd-creds encrypts the typed value with the host key or TPM2; a root materialiser writes the service's podman secret store",
        "the container reads /run/secrets/<KEY> by default; a snapshot never carries credentials"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "State and snapshots",
      "items": [
        "weedr creates each declared state volume as a btrfs subvolume; soil writes its own snapper configuration",
        "a routine snapshot is timeline-tagged and ages up the ladder; an on-demand one is number-tagged",
        "weedr snapshots every state volume while the service keeps running",
        "fork and rollback clone copy-on-write from a recorded per-volume number set; a bulk volume is never cloned",
        "retention belongs to snapper: guarden writes marks, never a delete loop"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Pins",
      "items": [
        "stakes writes one file per <service>:<volume>@<number>, with no shared index and no lock",
        "weedr pin sync runs root-side under one snapshots lock and writes important=yes",
        "a pin is a priority with a budget: under disk pressure a marked snapshot can still be reaped"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Host substrate",
      "items": [
        "soil phases: packages, storage, sysctl, firewall, install, units",
        "ferm is the only firewall; route_localnet plus nat DNAT forwards 80/tcp, 443/tcp and 443/udp",
        "the kernel owns 80 and 443; every service binds only an allocated loopback publication",
        "soil units installs the nightly snapshot timer and the pin-sync path unit, and the btrfs conversion spans two reboots"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Modules",
      "items": [
        "gate-traefik ships traefik-production and switches roots on",
        "homepage ships homepage-production and switches twig on",
        "cloudflared is an optional outbound terminator with no forwarded port",
        "modules talk through documented root-owned files and write none of each other's"
      ]
    }
  ]
